{"name":"Eggshell Pongee","hex":"#bea582","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eggshell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shell around an egg.","A pale off-white colour, like that of the eggshell of many chickens."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-whitish colour, like that of the eggshell.","Exhibiting the thinness, translucency or near-transparency, and fragility of an eggshell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eggshell"},{"term":"pongee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft unbleached silk, from China or India, from silkworms that feed on oak leaves.","A pale, yellowish shade of brown similar to beige."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Channa striata (striped snakehead)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pongee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eggshell","blocks":[{"text":"An eggshell is the outer covering of a hard-shelled egg and of some forms of eggs with soft outer cots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Egg-rmh.jpg/330px-Egg-rmh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggshell"},{"title":"Pongee","blocks":[{"text":"Pongee is a type of slub-woven fabric, created by weaving with yarns that have been spun by varying the tightness of the yarn's twist at various intervals. Pongee is typically made from silk, and results in a textured, \"slubbed\" appearance; pongee silks range from appearing similar to satin to appearing matte and unreflective. Though pongee is typically made out of silk, it can be woven from a variety of fabrics, such as cotton, linen and wool. Originally pongee was hand woven."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/%E8%A5%BF%E6%B9%96%E7%BB%B8%E4%BC%9E.jpg/330px-%E8%A5%BF%E6%B9%96%E7%BB%B8%E4%BC%9E.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pongee"